body:
I think it would make sense that the currentRefinedValues widget shows when a geo feature is used, either area filtering or search around a point.

I'm not sure how this should be done though, as displaying lat/lng coordinates does not make sense.
A quick hack is to provide a function for the template option and have an external source for the label to display depending on the coordinates/area filtering that is used.

Something like this:

```js
instantsearch.widgets.currentRefinedValues({
                        container: '#active-filters',
                        clearAll: false,
                        attributes: [
                            {
                                name: '_geoloc',
                                label: 'Location',
                                template: function(a) {
                                    return SomeObject.currentLocation;
                                }
                            }
                        ]
                       })
```

Thoughts?
